<speak>Separating keepsakes from practical records sounds like a good compromise. You don't have to choose between keeping a meaningful note and having a usable household drawer. A small dedicated place for those items can make them easier to enjoy, rather than finding them only when you're looking for a manual. For any formal records, follow the relevant retention guidance rather than treating them like ordinary clutter. If you're uncertain about a particular document, set it aside for a proper check instead of making a quick decision while tidying.</speak>